# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# KCD, 73 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, and a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine, 2026-10-22, build fda4ec7; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 43.3 s to 4397.2 s
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description KCD, 73 min of real streamed gameplay, b:vsync on the defaults (source rate not declared, 60 assumed; comb lock, 75 ms extra lag, flip timing and dejitter on) with capture through Windows.Graphics.Capture (-wgc), the mouse pointer in the picture and the frames that change less than a tenth of the largest area changed in the last half second left out, the frame pool on a device of its own and its textures opened on the present's device, and a frame shown as it is presented through the GPU's copy engine, 2026-10-22, build fda4ec7; cut to the stretch the stream's video shows, 43.3 s to 4397.2 s
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 14
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.8
field_pull_wraps 100
# WHAT IT COVERS: the second stream of 2026-10-22, from a relay launch of its own, 72.6 minutes
# cut to the gameplay its video shows, captured as the 2026-10-21 streams were (Windows.Graphics.
# Capture, the mouse pointer in the picture, the small-change frames left out, the pool on a
# device of its own) and presented through the GPU's copy engine: 263209 of the log's 266632
# presents were copied there, 3423 drawn, none failed. The policy is the one the tree ships. The
# game hitched (20 to 100 ms) 619 times (512 an hour), the most of any stream here, and stalled
# for 100 ms or more 58 times (48 an hour), in 129 bursts, 33 of them with a stall, and with no
# periodic stretch. The lock released 4 times, in the field and on the replay at the same
# moments: 1207.84, 1218.39, 2413.49 and 2857.62 s. The replay's worst blend run, 22 presents
# from 2413.6 s, starts at the third release, just after a burst of 11 hitches and 3 stalls
# (longest 192 ms) that ends at 2413.1 s. Of the 59 moves on the replay, 7 land more than 2 ms
# from a real frame.
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 43.328 s, from the 2831
# marked frames in its first 47 s, all on time and within 0.41 ms of that offset (p90). The video
# runs 4353.9 s with no holes, opens on gameplay on horseback and ends on gameplay after the
# sleep wheel and the inventory, so the cut is the whole video, 43.3 s to 4397.2 s of log time,
# and the marked frames lie inside it. Every second inside the cut that falls out of the 60 fps
# regime is a hitch second, 19 of them in 19 runs, none longer than 2 s, so nothing was removed
# from the middle.
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay line (the plain arm) reads synth 0.7% against 0.8%, worst run 22 against 14, runs >= 50
# 0 against 0 and pull wraps 80 against 100. On the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran and
# what the counts here use, blends are 2058 against 2065, repeats 497 against 498, skips 142
# against 140, pull wraps 100 against 100 and the worst run 22 against 14. The worst run is the
# one number outside the corpus's fidelity limits, by the same mechanism as on the first stream
# of the day: after the burst ending at 2413.1 s the field held its blends short and wrapped its
# pull at 2416.0 s, while the replay blended 22 presents in a row. The bound on the worst run
# holds the replay's own 22, so it still catches a change that lengthens it. The replay makes 59
# moves, 22 of them late, and the field's log has 64 in the window.
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 22
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.1
min_reseeds 197
max_pull_wraps 80
extra_lag_ms 75
arrivals 520089
